		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Change the value of max_function_arg]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=24230#p24230"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Hi again,</p><p>I have a Stored Proc in PostgreSQL which now has more than 100 args. When I try to create this STP, I get an error &quot;ERROR: functions cannot have more than 100 arguments&quot;.</p><p>I see that there is a Preset Option called &quot;max_function_args&quot; whose value is set to 100 by default. </p><p>Can someone tell me how to change the value of this &quot;max_function_args&quot; parameter (if possible) so that I can create the stored proc OR any other way to do the same?</p><p>Thanks.</p>]]></content>
